## When the user asks to document code

**On-demand only.** Run this workflow when the user invokes **`/y-dev-code-docs`**, **`@y-dev-code-docs`**, or clearly asks to document code (add docstrings, improve comments, fill documentation gaps). Do **not** run the gates below on casual Python edits — apply only the **standards** sections above.

**Do not** auto-commit. Hand off to **`/y-git-commits`** if the user wants commits.

### AskQuestion gates (mandatory)

Every decision must use **`AskQuestion`** — not chat-only prompts. Do **not** edit files until Steps 0–2 are answered (plus large-scope confirmation and removal second gate when triggered).

| Step | When | Select |
|------|------|--------|
| **0 — Scope** | Start of workflow | Single-select |
| **Large scope** | After Step 0 when triggers match | Single-select (pre-select **Narrow scope**) |
| **1 — Intent** | After scope confirmed | Multi-select (pre-select **Fill gaps**) |
| **2 — Depth** | After Step 1 | Multi-select (pre-select **Main members** + **Targeted block comments**) |
| **Removal confirm** | Step 1 includes **Remove redundant** | Single-select |

Mirror the gate pattern in [`y-git-commits.mdc`](../git/y-git-commits.mdc).

### Gather context (before Step 0)

Run read-only discovery as needed:

```bash
git status --short
git diff
git diff --staged
git log @{upstream}..HEAD --oneline
```

Pre-select Step 0 when obvious: `@` paths → user-specified; uncommitted `.py` in session → current task local changes; “my commits” → latest unpushed commits.

### Step 0 — Scope (single-select)

| Option | Scope |
|--------|--------|
| **Current task local changes** | Staged + unstaged `.py` in the working tree |
| **User-specified files or directories** | Paths from the message or `@` references |
| **Latest unpushed local commits** | Combined diff `@{upstream}..HEAD` (or `origin/<branch>..HEAD`) |
| **`other`** | User describes scope in chat |

Only **`.py`** files unless the user widens scope in `other`.

### Large-scope guardrail

After Step 0, count `.py` files in scope and list root paths. If **any** trigger applies, **`AskQuestion`** before Step 1 — state file count and roots in the prompt.

**Triggers:** user asked for entire project / whole repo / all Python; scope is repo root or a full top-level tree (`app/`, `src/`, etc.); **more than 10** `.py` files; unpushed-commits scope with **more than 10** `.py` files in the combined diff.

| Option | Action |
|--------|--------|
| **Narrow scope** (recommended) | Re-run Step 0 smaller |
| **Proceed with full scope** | Continue to Step 1 — user accepts risk |
| **Cancel** | Stop without edits |

### Step 1 — Intent (multi-select)

| Option | Default | Behavior |
|--------|---------|----------|
| **Fill gaps** | Yes | Add or **complete** docstrings and comments — missing **or incomplete** per **Incomplete docstrings** |
| **Revise existing code docs** | — | Improve clarity and wording on docstrings that already meet structural standards |
| **Remove redundant or outdated docs** | — | Shorten or delete redundant narration only; second gate required |

**Order when multiple:** fill gaps → revise → remove redundant.

**Fill gaps** — treat as a gap when the docstring is absent **or** incomplete (thin one-liner on a non-trivial API, missing required `Args` / `Returns` / `Raises`, non-Google prose). Bring each symbol in scope to the minimum bar in **Docstrings** and **Incomplete docstrings**. Do not skip a symbol only because it already has a one-line docstring.

**Revise existing** — prose and clarity only; does not replace **Fill gaps** for missing sections.

**Remove redundant — hard rules:**

- Never remove debug, `TODO`, `FIXME`, or investigation comments unless the user confirms in the **removal second gate**.
- Never remove comments that explain **why** or business rules.
- On **public API**, prefer tightening docstrings over deleting them.

### Removal second gate

Only when **Remove redundant** is selected. Single-select: redundant docstrings only / redundant inline narration only / both / cancel clean pass.

### Step 2 — Depth (multi-select)

| Option | Default | Behavior |
|--------|---------|----------|
| **Main members** | Yes | Module, class, public function/method docstrings — no inline logic comments |
| **Targeted block comments** | Yes | Unclear or complicated blocks only; skip obvious code |
| **Verbose walkthrough (not recommended)** | No | Line-level comments on most statements for session understanding; skip trivial lines |

**Verbose mode:**

- Temporary help for the **current developer** — not production documentation.
- **Do not commit** verbose-only changes unless the user explicitly asks to commit afterward.
- Note in the handoff: verbose comments are local/temp — review before commit.
- Plain prose only; no reST markup.

### Apply

- Follow all **standards** sections above for every edit.
- Under **Fill gaps**, scan each main member in scope against **Incomplete docstrings** — do not treat an existing one-liner as done when sections or prose are still required.
- Respect **`y-agt-debug-comments`** throughout.
- If **verbose** and **remove redundant** are both selected: add verbose first; clean pass must not strip new verbose comments without removal-gate confirmation.
- End with a short summary: files touched, intents applied, commit-ready vs temp-only.

